          "This module assesses whether the paper's code could be run on its data. It performs static analysis only here: **no code is run**. We examined 2 R code files.",
          "#### Run order",
          "The scripts were ordered by their data dependencies (a script writing a file another reads runs first), `source()` calls, and numeric filename prefixes. **1 `source()` reference** only matched a file after normalising both names (lowercase, extension stripped, a leading numbering prefix stripped, separators collapsed) — a likely renumbered/reworded filename rather than an exact match: `02_analysis.R` -> `01_clean.R`. Treat these as lower-confidence than an exact `source()` resolution.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Order = 1:2, File = c(\"01_clean.R\", \"02_analysis.R\"\n), \"Runs after\" = c(\"—\", \"01_clean.R\"), Basis = c(\"numeric\", \n\"dependency\")), row.names = c(NA, -2L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
